  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather will continue through the rest of the \nweek with a day to day warming trend.\n\nWidespread stratus will persist this afternoon across Western and \nCentral NY, with some sunshine across the North Country. The low \nstratus will gradually shrink in coverage tonight, although some \nlake effect clouds will persist overnight east of the lakes. The \nlast of the lake effect clouds should dissipate Tuesday morning as \ntemperatures aloft become too warm to support lake effect clouds.\n\nA strong mid/upper level ridge will build over the eastern 1/3 of \nthe CONUS through midweek, and then persist through the rest of the \nweek as a longwave trough becomes established across the west. \nStrong surface high pressure will remain centered from the Ohio \nValley to the mid Atlantic through the rest of the week before \ndrifting off the east coast Saturday.\n\nThe strong high pressure surface and aloft will support dry weather \nand a good deal of sunshine each day Tuesday through Saturday. A day \nto day warming trend will boost temperatures to well above average \nfrom midweek through Saturday.",
